    },
    {
      "id": "fca43f10-12b3-4b38-894f-019322a88808",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "Please note that this is an optional waiver program AND a track in the Kinesiology B.A. This agreement displays all lower-division courses required in the program : Stanislaus State courses or requirements on the left, approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right. Helpful resources: Academic Catalog Transfer Admissions Questions regarding this agreement may be directed to the Stanislaus State Articulation Analyst. Please visit the Stanislaus State Articulation Website for contact information.",
      "contentHtml": "<h2><strong style=\"font-size: 20px; color: rgb(29, 32, 36);\">Please note that this is an optional waiver program <u>AND</u> a track in the </strong><a href=\"https://catalog.csustan.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=32&amp;poid=7151&amp;returnto=5379\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 20px; color: rgb(29, 32, 36);\"><strong>Kinesiology B.A.</strong></a><strong style=\"font-size: 20px; color: rgb(29, 32, 36);\">&nbsp;</strong></h2><p><br></p><p>This agreement displays all<strong> lower-division courses required in the program</strong>: Stanislaus State courses or requirements on the left, approved (articulated) transfer courses on the right.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Helpful resources: </strong></p><p><a href=\"https://catalog.csustan.edu/index.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Academic Catalog</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.csustan.edu/undergrad/transfer-admission\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer Admissions</a></p><p><br></p><p>Questions regarding this agreement may be directed to the Stanislaus State Articulation Analyst. Please visit the <a href=\"https://www.csustan.edu/articulation\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Stanislaus State Articulation Website</a> for contact information.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "4eec6545-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "About the Program",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8afb7845-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "This degree prepares students for admission to the Single Subject Credential Program in Physical Education ; The mission of the faculty of the Subject Matter Preparation Program (SMPP) is to prepare professionally exceptional physical education teachers and coaches that foster the acquisition of content knowledge and skills, and promote physically active lifestyles of children and young adults through high quality physical education programs. This degree path allows individuals to enter into a credential program. This single subject waiver program is designed for students who wish to enter credential programs in physical education for K-12 schools. The SMPP in Physical Education is approved by the California Commission on Teacher Credentialing and fulfills the subject matter competency prerequisite for entrance into a credential program for a single subject teaching credential in physical education. Please note that this is an optional waiver program and a track in the Kinesiology B.A. Students intending to enter the Credential Program should consult the Teacher Education section of the Academic Catalog for additional requirements. View information for the Department of Kinesiology and Public Health Promotion , including Learning Objectives for the department and its programs.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>This degree prepares students for admission to the <a href=\"https://catalog.csustan.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=35&amp;poid=7905\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Single Subject Credential Program in Physical Education</a>; The mission of the faculty of the Subject Matter Preparation Program (SMPP) is to prepare professionally exceptional physical education teachers and coaches that foster the acquisition of content knowledge and skills, and promote physically active lifestyles of children and young adults through high quality physical education programs. This degree path allows individuals to enter into a credential program.</p><p><br></p><p>This single subject waiver program is designed for students who wish to enter credential programs in physical education for K-12 schools. The SMPP in Physical Education is approved by the California Commission on Teacher Credentialing and fulfills the subject matter competency prerequisite for entrance into a credential program for a single subject teaching credential in physical education.</p><p><br></p><p>Please note that this is an optional waiver program <strong><u>and</u> </strong>a track in the Kinesiology B.A. Students intending to enter the Credential Program should consult the <a href=\"https://catalog.csustan.edu/preview_entity.php?catoid=35&amp;ent_oid=1713\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Teacher Education</a> section of the <a href=\"https://catalog.csustan.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Academic Catalog</a> for additional requirements.</p><p><br></p><p>View information for the <a href=\"https://catalog.csustan.edu/preview_entity.php?catoid=35&amp;ent_oid=1711\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Department of Kinesiology and Public Health Promotion</a>, including Learning Objectives for the department and its programs.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "50137745-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "about lower division major requirements",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "a23a7445-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 5,
      "content": "Each course counted toward the major, including prerequisites, must be completed with a grade of C- (1.7) or higher. All courses counted toward the major (both within and outside of the Department) must be taken on a letter grade basis.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>Each course counted toward the major, including prerequisites, must be completed with a grade of C- (1.7) or higher. All courses counted toward the major (both within and outside of the Department) must be taken on a letter grade basis.</p>"
    }
